From 35cbad2d661d066c2d4bee84fc8001162496853e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:27:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [MSE] Accept a SourceBuffer type the element's CDM decodes

MediaSource.isTypeSupported() cannot tell encrypted from clear media,
so it refuses a codec that no decoder for clear media takes, or that
only a software decoder takes under the
media-content-types-requiring-hardware-support setting, and
addSourceBuffer() then refuses it as well, even for a page that has set
MediaKeys whose CDM decodes that codec itself. addSourceBuffer() now
also accepts a type whose video the CDM of the media element's MediaKeys
claims, asked through CDM and MediaKeys, with the container left to the
media engine. The GStreamer append pipeline, which checks each track of
an initialization segment for a decoder for clear media, accepts an
encrypted video track the same way: when the CDM instance attached to
the player claims its media type, and the protection system the demuxer
names for the track, if any, is that instance's. isTypeSupported() keeps
its answer, which pages use to choose formats for clear media too.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
